NAME
    rm - remove writable filesystem objects

SYNOPSIS
    rm FILE
    rm -r DIRECTORY
    rm -R DIRECTORY

DESCRIPTION
    Removes one regular file or symbolic link from a writable provider.
    Removing one ext4 hard-link name preserves the inode and its other names.
    With -r or -R, traverses directories iteratively in post-order and never
    follows symbolic links. Roots, mountpoints, immutable content, and mounted
    read-only content are rejected.
